 "text": "Hey, how can I help you? On a laptop, refresh rate refers to the number of times a screen's pixels are redrawn or updated per second. Yes, higher refresh rates are better because they prevent screen tearing and produce smoother, more fluid motion. It doesn't directly drain the battery, but it does use more power because it's redrawing the screen constantly. For watching videos and content, a higher refresh rate can be more noticeable with smoother, cleaner motion. It's also important for gaming as it reduces lag and improves response time.",
